    "body": "## Python test detection\n\nCheckWash 0.13.1 reports `TEST_PATCHES_SUBJECT` when an existing Python test keeps its direct equality assertion but a new same-named local function supplies the value in place of the imported project function. The billing example in #635 now blocks at the default threshold. The patch also covers the reviewed numeric pytest fixture that returns the result of calling its local replacement. [Merged fix](https://github.com/taipei49314/checkwash/pull/640) · [Coverage and limits](https://github.com/taipei49314/checkwash/blob/v0.13.1/docs/KNOWN-ISSUES-v0.13.1.md)\n\nThe fixed 3,600-commit comparison against the published 0.13.0 zipapp produced identical exit codes and output for every pair, including the two established symlink errors. The original #635 example was tested separately. [Release guide](https://github.com/taipei49314/checkwash/blob/v0.13.1/docs/releases/v0.13.1-public-launch.md)\n\nThe annotated tag points to Action commit `62656df812372c085b4d32c7864fcdfaccd0318a`. The release merge is `5e2a89ef0d447ae6e08c289f4a3357325b7286e9`. [Tag verification](https://github.com/taipei49314/checkwash/runs/137093644288) · [Cross-platform source verification](https://github.com/taipei49314/checkwash/actions/runs/44970495987)\r\n",
